Electron adaptation notes (44-x-y):
This reland is a revert-of-a-revert whose 3-way base is far from M152, so
several hunks were hand-resolved:
- bad_message.h / stability enums.xml: the two new BadMessageReason values
  are numbered 366/367 (next free on this branch) instead of upstream's
  372/373; the intermediate upstream enum entries are not present here.
- public_url_manager.cc: the is_stopped_ checks and the pending_remote
  validity check were applied onto M152's include set (added features.h,
  local_frame.h, local_frame_client.h); other include-list drift ignored.
- url_file_api.cc: this branch calls DOMURL::CreatePublicURL (upstream
  renamed it to URL::CreatePublicURL); only the explanatory comment was
  added and it names the M152 function.
- Test-only files chrome/browser/site_isolation/
  chrome_site_per_process_browsertest.cc and public_url_manager_test.cc
  were dropped (Electron does not build chrome/; the blink unit test's
  include set diverged). blob_url_browsertest.cc applied cleanly.
The browser-side checks, the blink feature flag, local_frame.cc and
worklet_global_scope.* hunks are verbatim upstream.

